const PRACTICE_RULE_EN = "The practice rule for every exercise: always inside the bandage or sleeve, at an effort no higher than 'somewhat hard' (Campbell 2019); the PAL symptom rule: the arm starts with no weight or half a kilogram and rises 0.25–0.5 kg a week if heaviness, swelling and aching have not changed since the previous week, if symptoms increase the exercise is skipped or lightened until they settle, and after two or more missed sessions it restarts lighter (Schmitz 2009b); if symptoms last more than a week or volume rises 5% above the last measurement (the Wong 2024 threshold), arm resistance is stopped, the garment and skin are checked and the limb is re-measured (a proposal combining the two); the leg starts without weights, and any redness or heat → the cellulitis rule (Katz 2010); and the limb is measured by the same method and the same assessor every time (Levenhagen 2017).";
const EXTEND_AR = "وفي الجلسة ١٨: تمديدٌ واحد بستّ جلسات (حتى ٢٤) لا غير، وبالمعيار المكتوب وحده: نقص حجمُ الطرف أكثرَ من ٣٪ بين الجلسة ١٢ والجلسة ١٨ — فما زال الاحتقانُ يزول، وخطأُ القياس ١٫٩–٣٫٢٪ (Deltombe 2007) — والحجمُ الزائد ما زال ١٠٪ فأكثر (Levenhagen 2017)؛ ولا تمديدَ لمن ثبت حجمُه، فالجلساتُ الأكثر لا تزيد النقصَ وتُضعف الالتزامَ في البيت (Mondry 2004 · Liao 2012)، وأكثرُ مَن يحتاجه وذمةُ الساق والمرحلةُ الثالثة (اقتراحٌ بلا تجربة). ثمّ الخروجُ عند الثبات بالملبس المقيس والعناية الذاتية، ومراجعاتٌ بعد شهر — فأكبرُ الزيادة المبكّرة بلا ضغط الليل (Mestre 2017) — ثمّ ٣ و٦ و١٢ شهراً ثمّ كلَّ ٦–١٢ شهراً (Wong 2024)؛ وكتلةٌ جديدة إن زاد الحجمُ أكثرَ من ١٠٪ فوق قيمة الخروج — وقد بلغها ٥٢٪ في سنة (Vignes 2007) — أو بعد التهابٍ خلويّ، والزيادةُ ٥ إلى أقلّ من ١٠٪ ⟵ مراجعةُ الملبس (Wong 2024). والبديلُ لمن لا تحضر يومياً: ثلاثٌ في الأسبوع ستّةَ أسابيع (١٨ جلسة) والرباطُ القابل للتعديل تضعه بنفسها بين الجلسات (Gurdal 2012 · Sanal-Toprak 2019 · Damstra 2013).";
const EXTEND_EN = "At session 18: one extension of six sessions (to 24) and no more, by the written criterion only: limb volume fell by more than 3% between session 12 and session 18 — so decongestion is still going on, and the measurement error is 1.9–3.2% (Deltombe 2007) — and excess volume is still 10% or more (Levenhagen 2017); there is no extension for a volume that has plateaued, as more sessions add no reduction and weaken home adherence (Mondry 2004 · Liao 2012), and the likeliest users are leg lymphoedema and stage III (a proposal with no trial). Then discharge at the plateau with the measured garment and self-care, with reviews after one month — the largest early rise comes without night compression (Mestre 2017) — then at 3, 6 and 12 months and every 6–12 months after (Wong 2024); a new block if volume rises more than 10% above the discharge value — 52% reached that within a year (Vignes 2007) — or after cellulitis, and a rise of 5 to under 10% → a garment review (Wong 2024). The alternative for a patient who cannot attend daily: three a week for six weeks (18 sessions) with an adjustable wrap she applies herself between sessions (Gurdal 2012 · Sanal-Toprak 2019 · Damstra 2013).";

